With a single Grassmann generator and ordinary coefficient $a$, $e^{a\theta}
=1+a\theta,$ because every higher power vanishes. Two exponentials involving the same generator obey $\begin{aligned}e^{a\theta}e^{b\theta}
&=(1+a\theta)(1+b\theta)\\
&=1+(a+b)\theta\\
&=e^{(a+b)\theta}.\end{aligned}$

